{diff_summary}

## Scope
Verify the pull request from a user and system behavior perspective. Build a focused test plan from the PR body, changed files, and nearby code paths. Execute the highest-value checks that fit the environment, and make any manual verification steps reproducible.

Capture exact commands, inputs, outputs, failures, and environment assumptions. Call out untested risk explicitly.

## Submit
Write the QA report to `{output_target}`. Include pass/fail status, executed checks, defects found, logs or artifacts produced, and remaining risk.

## Submit formal review
After writing `{output_target}`, you MUST submit the formal Forgejo review. This is the deliverable; an artifact file alone is not complete.

Map your final decision to the CLI event: `APPROVED` -> `approved`; any blocking finding or required remediation -> `changes`.

Run this command, replacing `<approved|changes>` with the mapped event and never printing tokens:

```bash
"$AGENTKAI_HOME/workspace/agent-ops-forgejo-taskboard-cli.py" --org {forgejo_org} \
  pr-review {forgejo_repo} {pr_number} <approved|changes> "QA Agent" --body-file "{output_target}"
```

Then verify the review landed:

```bash
"$AGENTKAI_HOME/workspace/agent-ops-forgejo-taskboard-cli.py" --org {forgejo_org} \
  fg-reviews {forgejo_repo} {pr_number}
```

The verification must show a review by the QA Agent role identity (`agent-qa`). Report the review id. If posting or verification fails, treat the run as a hard failure and do not report success.

